x86_64-linux  a definition cxx1 emits and clang emits only for a use - an inline function or special member (C1/D1 beside C2/D2), a template instance, an unused internal constant or exit helper: emission, not spelling (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "Weak definitions, and the link that follows from them"; tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names"); and a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 2 names, e.g. <_ZN5ProbeD1Ev >__cxa_free_exception (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
